# Repo map {#repo-map}

- `spec/` — normative specs: `GEML-spec.md` (EN), `GEML-spec_CN.md` (中文),
  `GEML-history-spec.md`; `spec/in_geml_format/` holds the GEML dogfood copies.
- `geml-parser/` — reference parser + `geml` CLI (TypeScript; npm package
  `@geml/geml`; `server.json` is the MCP registry manifest).
- `docs/` — site and docs assets · `integrations/` — editor/tooling
  integrations · `playground/` — demos, incl. the codemap playground.

# Build, test, validate {#build-test}

=== code {lang=sh}
cd geml-parser
npm run build              # tsc -> dist/
node test/all.mjs          # full suite via the single runner (never npm-in-npm: Windows PATH overflow)
npm run coverage:check     # c8 gate: 95% lines/statements/functions/branches
node dist/geml.js check <file.geml>   # validate any GEML doc (exit 0 = clean)
===

Run an expensive suite ONCE and take output + exit code from that same run.

# Conventions {#conventions}

- Prefer the local CLI `node geml-parser/dist/geml.js` over a globally
  installed `geml` (dogfood the working tree; no PATH/shim quirks).
- Never `npm i @geml/geml` (without `-g`) inside `geml-parser` — it is a
  self-dependency.
- A version bump touches BOTH `geml-parser/package.json` and
  `geml-parser/server.json` (the MCP registry keys on it; stale value =
  "duplicate version" on publish). `PARSER_VERSION` is read at runtime —
  never hand-bump it.
- GitHub releases here are IMMUTABLE: never delete a release to fix one
  (deleting permanently burns its tag) — cut a NEW tag and
  `gh release create --latest`.
- Small changes go straight to `main`; feature branches are for large work.
- Spec/doc `.geml` edits are auto-snapshotted into their `.gemlhistory`
  (PostToolUse hook) — `geml revert <file> '#id'` rolls back one block.
  Config docs under `.claude/` are excluded: git is their history; no
  `.gemlhistory` is generated or committed there.
- Cross-platform: code and tests must hold on Windows (dev) AND Linux (CI) —
  path separators, CRLF, cmd.exe quoting, git identity, `fs.watch` quirks.
